The technical cause (simplified code)
// Simplified illustration -- not the actual flight code (which was in Ada)
double horizontal_bias = compute_bias(sensor_data);  // 64-bit float

// Protected conversions checked the range first.
// This one was left unprotected:
int16_t bh = (int16_t) horizontal_bias;  // fine on Ariane 4 trajectories,
                                         // overflows on Ariane 5

Seven variables were at risk of overflow; four were protected, three were not
Why? To keep the SRI computer’s workload under a target of 80%, and because analysis showed those values were physically limited for Ariane 4
